WEBVTT

00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:21.180
This isn't enough speed!

00:00:22.110 --> 00:00:25.120
Overcome your limits, Yusei!

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:30.040
To reach new limits, I need a new engine.

00:00:48.940 --> 00:00:54.080
Every time you're hurt, you can become kinder

00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:59.610
Stand up and you'll understand strength

00:00:59.950 --> 00:01:04.090
Don't look back and keep going

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:09.920
Both the past and the future 
are connected to the present

00:01:10.090 --> 00:01:14.900
There's no need to fear

00:01:15.130 --> 00:01:22.570
I'll keep telling you that you're not alone

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:28.580
The passionate emotions in your heart

00:01:29.310 --> 00:01:34.350
Streak to the infinite future

00:01:34.550 --> 00:01:39.750
Dreams surpass their limits

00:01:40.020 --> 00:01:47.860
And will lead you to a bright place

00:02:14.460 --> 00:02:20.240
The Mysterious Super Mechanic

00:02:28.180 --> 00:02:31.890
I don't know why you're doing 
this, but thanks for the treat!

00:02:31.890 --> 00:02:33.930
Eat up, Yusei.

00:02:33.930 --> 00:02:36.830
Jack, you'll rarely get 
to eat such a fine meal!

00:02:37.020 --> 00:02:38.300
I'm suspicious.

00:02:39.130 --> 00:02:41.770
About what, Master Atlas?

00:02:41.770 --> 00:02:46.030
Martha said that there's nothing 
more expensive than free.

00:02:46.030 --> 00:02:49.770
Appreciate people who speak harshly to you.

00:02:49.770 --> 00:02:52.620
Be careful of people who sweet talk you.

00:02:52.790 --> 00:02:55.060
Yusei's right.

00:02:55.060 --> 00:02:59.260
They have low salaries!  They're treating 
us because they have an ulterior motive!

00:02:59.430 --> 00:03:01.220
Why do you think that?

00:03:01.220 --> 00:03:03.150
There's no ulterior motive?

00:03:03.150 --> 00:03:04.930
Well, umm...

00:03:05.380 --> 00:03:07.640
We want a favor.

00:03:07.640 --> 00:03:09.130
So there was a motive.

00:03:09.130 --> 00:03:11.700
It's nothing big.

00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:14.500
We took an amnesiac into 
custody the other day.

00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:17.340
We want you to take care of him for awhile.

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:19.390
Why do we have to do that?

00:03:19.390 --> 00:03:25.080
Due to tourists and D-Wheelers, our hands 
are full maintaining Neo Domino City.

00:03:25.270 --> 00:03:27.090
Just for a little while.

00:03:27.090 --> 00:03:29.250
Our garage is not a hotel!

00:03:29.900 --> 00:03:33.550
We don't have time to 
take care of a stranger.

00:03:33.550 --> 00:03:34.990
Please, Yusei.

00:03:34.990 --> 00:03:35.660
I refuse.

00:03:35.840 --> 00:03:37.830
Please, Master Atlas.

00:03:37.830 --> 00:03:38.500
I refuse!

00:03:38.710 --> 00:03:39.960
Please!

00:03:40.120 --> 00:03:41.200
I refuse!

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:46.390
Crow, you're refusing after 
eating this high-quality steak?

00:03:46.390 --> 00:03:48.440
You got me there.

00:03:48.440 --> 00:03:51.330
Where is this person?

00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:54.670
He should be here by now...

00:03:55.050 --> 00:03:58.070
If he's not here, there's nothing we can do.

00:04:01.150 --> 00:04:02.660
That was close.

00:04:02.660 --> 00:04:05.250
We almost had to take care of a stranger.

00:04:05.250 --> 00:04:10.830
That's because you started eating quickly 
even though you're not a professional speed eater!

00:04:10.830 --> 00:04:14.300
But I may never eat at such 
a nice restaurant again!

00:04:14.750 --> 00:04:17.140
You're a good kid.

00:04:17.140 --> 00:04:19.600
I'll also wipe this stain off.

00:04:19.600 --> 00:04:21.010
Now you're clean!

00:04:21.010 --> 00:04:23.910
What are you doing to my D-Wheel?

00:04:24.440 --> 00:04:28.160
You're in the gang that steals D-Wheels!

00:04:29.570 --> 00:04:32.400
Don't come near my D-Wheel again!

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:34.640
Or you'll end up worse next time!

00:04:35.170 --> 00:04:36.530
Jack!

00:04:40.020 --> 00:04:42.200
What's with Jack?

00:04:43.040 --> 00:04:44.870
Are you okay?  Hang in there!

00:04:44.870 --> 00:04:46.380
Leave him alone.

00:04:46.380 --> 00:04:47.570
I can't do that.

00:04:49.780 --> 00:04:51.250
What's going on?

00:04:51.250 --> 00:04:52.490
What happened?

00:04:52.490 --> 00:04:54.210
It's not Jack's fault.

00:04:54.400 --> 00:04:57.520
He tried to steal Wheel of Fortune.

00:04:57.830 --> 00:04:59.190
It's you!

00:04:59.190 --> 00:05:00.290
Bruno!

00:05:00.290 --> 00:05:02.560
What are you doing here?

00:05:02.560 --> 00:05:03.780
Sorry.

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:07.120
It was an incredible D-Wheel, 
so I wanted to touch it.

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:10.430
The person you wanted us to take care of...

00:05:10.430 --> 00:05:11.590
It's him.

00:05:11.590 --> 00:05:13.170
Are you serious?

00:05:13.170 --> 00:05:14.770
What should we do, Yusei?

00:05:14.770 --> 00:05:16.560
What is there to do?

00:05:18.160 --> 00:05:19.740
Master Atlas!

00:05:19.740 --> 00:05:22.160
I'm borrowing him tonight!

00:05:22.160 --> 00:05:24.520
What's going on?

00:05:24.520 --> 00:05:25.660
After him, Crow!

00:05:25.660 --> 00:05:27.140
Yusei!

00:05:27.640 --> 00:05:29.500
Leave the rest to us!

00:05:38.720 --> 00:05:40.990
Please stop!  I'm against violence!

00:05:41.200 --> 00:05:43.560
Jack, why are you suddenly acting like this?

00:05:43.560 --> 00:05:44.730
Spill the beans!

00:05:44.730 --> 00:05:47.120
What did you do to my Wheel of Fortune?

00:05:47.120 --> 00:05:48.690
What do you mean, Jack?

00:05:49.290 --> 00:05:52.090
Wheel of Fortune has more power.

00:05:52.090 --> 00:05:53.130
What?

00:05:53.130 --> 00:05:57.540
I only fiddled with that 
D-Wheel's computer data.

00:05:57.540 --> 00:05:58.830
Impossible!

00:05:58.830 --> 00:06:03.680
Yusei is having a lot of trouble 
increasing our D-Wheels' power.

00:06:03.680 --> 00:06:06.180
But he did it in a short time?

00:06:06.180 --> 00:06:08.500
That's the only explanation!

00:06:09.060 --> 00:06:11.580
Can you teach me how you did it?

00:06:16.330 --> 00:06:20.330
This is where I adjusted 
the boost timing setting.

00:06:20.330 --> 00:06:22.570
That powers it up a bit.

00:06:22.570 --> 00:06:24.960
I see.  I never noticed that.

00:06:24.960 --> 00:06:26.240
What are they talking about?

00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:27.500
I have no idea.

00:06:27.500 --> 00:06:28.980
But don't let your guard down.

00:06:28.980 --> 00:06:31.500
We still don't know if he's friendly.

00:06:31.500 --> 00:06:34.930
This will also work for 
Yusei and Crow's D-Wheels.

00:06:34.930 --> 00:06:37.930
If you adjust the program, they'll 
have more power than before.

00:06:38.390 --> 00:06:39.620
Really?

00:06:39.620 --> 00:06:42.140
Crow, didn't you hear what I said?

00:06:42.140 --> 00:06:44.220
I'll adjust it right away.

00:06:44.590 --> 00:06:46.110
I'm counting on you!

00:06:47.250 --> 00:06:48.950
What's your name again?

00:06:49.160 --> 00:06:51.660
My name is Bruno.

00:06:51.660 --> 00:06:52.780
My name is-

00:06:52.780 --> 00:06:56.460
I already know.  You're Yusei, Crow and Jack.

00:06:56.460 --> 00:07:00.130
Bruno, since I trust your skills, 
I want you to look at this.

00:07:00.300 --> 00:07:02.290
I'm having a hard time controlling it.

00:07:02.290 --> 00:07:05.840
This Moment Engine is 
made of Yusei Particles.

00:07:06.030 --> 00:07:07.570
Have you already built a real version?

00:07:07.570 --> 00:07:09.180
Not yet.

00:07:09.180 --> 00:07:11.970
You're currently building 
the control program.

00:07:11.970 --> 00:07:14.490
That should be the priority.

00:07:14.490 --> 00:07:19.430
It's true that how you build D-Wheel Moment 
Engines can affect their output power.

00:07:19.430 --> 00:07:24.760
But since their basic structure is the same, 
the control program affects the speed more.

00:07:24.760 --> 00:07:28.030
Yusei, those are the new engine's blueprints!

00:07:28.030 --> 00:07:29.790
It's top secret!

00:07:29.790 --> 00:07:31.680
Don't interrupt, Jack!

00:07:31.680 --> 00:07:33.630
We're having a serious discussion!

00:07:33.630 --> 00:07:34.890
Wait a sec!

00:07:34.890 --> 00:07:37.700
So when we talk, we're not 
having a serious discussion?

00:07:37.910 --> 00:07:39.700
What if we do this?

00:07:39.700 --> 00:07:41.750
That should stabilize the power.

00:07:41.750 --> 00:07:42.820
Yusei?

00:07:42.820 --> 00:07:45.050
Let Yusei handle this.

00:07:45.050 --> 00:07:47.770
They're having a serious discussion.

00:07:48.050 --> 00:07:51.010
You too?  Do whatever you want!

00:07:51.010 --> 00:07:54.310
But if you do that, you're sacrificing power.

00:07:54.310 --> 00:07:55.880
That's the dilemma.

00:07:55.880 --> 00:07:57.080
I see.

00:07:57.080 --> 00:07:59.180
Then you can try this method.

00:07:59.180 --> 00:08:01.390
Like this, for example...

00:08:02.190 --> 00:08:05.900
Yusei is revitalized.

00:08:12.250 --> 00:08:14.670
I think this concept will work.

00:08:14.670 --> 00:08:16.570
Yeah, it's worth testing.

00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:18.580
Thank you, Bruno.

00:08:18.580 --> 00:08:20.580
I learned a lot from your ideas.

00:08:20.780 --> 00:08:24.680
It was only possible because 
your basic designs were solid.

00:08:24.680 --> 00:08:27.330
No wonder you're Professor Fudo's son.

00:08:27.330 --> 00:08:29.150
Can I eat this?

00:08:29.150 --> 00:08:31.360
You know about my father?

00:08:31.360 --> 00:08:36.090
Professor Fudo's Moment is the 
basis for all D-Wheel engines.

00:08:36.090 --> 00:08:39.060
Everyone who likes D-Wheels knows him.

00:08:39.440 --> 00:08:43.850
Yusei, were you named after the Yusei Gear?

00:08:43.850 --> 00:08:45.740
Something like that.

00:08:45.740 --> 00:08:47.940
So it's true?

00:08:47.940 --> 00:08:49.910
It's a unique name, after all.

00:08:52.980 --> 00:08:55.780
Yusei Gear has an interesting structure.

00:08:55.780 --> 00:08:58.150
As one gear, it's completely useless.

00:08:58.150 --> 00:09:02.150
The Sun Gear at the center ties 
together many other gears.

00:09:03.210 --> 00:09:08.140
If we're all individual gears, what's 
the Sun Gear that ties us together?

00:09:08.140 --> 00:09:09.280
I know.

00:09:09.280 --> 00:09:13.200
It's Duel Monsters because they 
make Riding Duels possible.

00:09:13.590 --> 00:09:17.200
Furthermore, there's a bond 
between us, Jack and Crow.

00:09:17.200 --> 00:09:20.610
I see.  That's a concise 
and beautiful structure.

00:09:20.610 --> 00:09:24.610
Bruno, Mikage said that you have amnesia.

00:09:25.360 --> 00:09:28.580
When I regained consciousness, 
I was on the shore.

00:09:28.580 --> 00:09:30.810
Were you in an accident?

00:09:30.810 --> 00:09:33.420
I don't remember.

00:09:33.420 --> 00:09:38.720
But when I'm working on D-Wheels or when 
I'm dueling, I feel like I'll remember.

00:09:39.240 --> 00:09:40.730
I see.

00:09:41.190 --> 00:09:45.480
Bruno, will you stay here for awhile?

00:09:45.730 --> 00:09:46.860
Is that okay?

00:09:46.860 --> 00:09:52.330
Yeah.  We need a new machine for the WRGP.

00:09:52.330 --> 00:09:53.850
I want your help.

00:09:54.440 --> 00:09:58.910
I'll be a gear that'll make 
your dreams come true.

00:09:58.910 --> 00:10:00.430
Thank you, Bruno.

00:10:01.650 --> 00:10:02.920
Same here.

00:10:08.420 --> 00:10:10.530
Yusei, let's play!

00:10:10.530 --> 00:10:13.110
Rua discovered a new combo!

00:10:13.390 --> 00:10:16.560
Yusei, can you help me 
with this physics problem?

00:10:18.300 --> 00:10:20.030
Who is he?

00:10:20.030 --> 00:10:23.340
He's a vagabond forced on us by 
the Public Maintenance Department.

00:10:23.340 --> 00:10:27.360
Yusei hired and promoted 
him to super mechanic.

00:10:27.360 --> 00:10:29.010
Super mechanic?

00:10:29.010 --> 00:10:31.900
Can he improve my Duel Board?

00:10:31.900 --> 00:10:33.350
Maybe.

00:10:33.350 --> 00:10:34.950
They're not bored.

00:10:34.950 --> 00:10:37.300
Are there that many topics to discuss?

00:10:37.970 --> 00:10:42.480
They've easily surpassed the number of 
conversations I've ever had with Yusei.

00:10:42.480 --> 00:10:44.020
They're like a pair of love birds.

00:10:44.020 --> 00:10:46.440
That term is only used 
between a man and a woman.

00:10:46.440 --> 00:10:47.450
Oh yeah.

00:10:47.820 --> 00:10:49.720
What's wrong, Aki?

00:10:50.690 --> 00:10:51.660
I'm going home.

00:10:51.660 --> 00:10:53.430
I'm only in the way if I stay here.

00:10:53.650 --> 00:10:56.450
Aki, are you jealous?

00:10:56.450 --> 00:10:59.670
Since you're a child, stop 
talking like an adult!

00:11:01.960 --> 00:11:04.140
Aki is seriously angry.

00:11:04.140 --> 00:11:06.140
Should we check on her?

00:11:06.140 --> 00:11:07.680
I don't know!

00:11:07.680 --> 00:11:09.170
Same here.

00:11:09.170 --> 00:11:14.850
Well, if this gets us one step closer to 
creating a new engine, it's a godsend.

00:11:26.980 --> 00:11:29.090
Seems good.  It'll work.

00:11:38.340 --> 00:11:39.690
It's finished!

00:11:39.690 --> 00:11:41.110
We did it, Yusei.

00:11:41.110 --> 00:11:42.900
This is a miraculous program.

00:11:42.900 --> 00:11:43.760
Yeah.

00:11:44.230 --> 00:11:46.770
I'm going to lie down for a while.

00:11:46.770 --> 00:11:48.910
I haven't slept in days, so I'm exhausted.

00:11:48.910 --> 00:11:50.300
Same here.

00:11:50.300 --> 00:11:52.600
We'll install this into the machine tomorrow.

00:12:26.390 --> 00:12:29.460
What?  Someone stole the data?

00:12:29.460 --> 00:12:30.650
We were careless.

00:12:30.650 --> 00:12:33.160
We should've made a backup.

00:12:33.160 --> 00:12:35.810
Yusei and I were both exhausted.

00:12:35.810 --> 00:12:36.630
It couldn't be helped.

00:12:36.850 --> 00:12:38.260
You're the thief!

00:12:38.260 --> 00:12:40.150
I was suspicious of you from the start!

00:12:40.150 --> 00:12:41.850
You're wrong!  It wasn't me!

00:12:41.850 --> 00:12:42.990
Wait, Jack!

00:12:42.990 --> 00:12:44.340
Don't stop me, Yusei!

00:12:44.340 --> 00:12:46.420
I'll uncover his identity!

00:12:46.420 --> 00:12:47.640
Stop it!

00:12:47.640 --> 00:12:49.850
You're also taking his side?

00:12:49.850 --> 00:12:51.620
It's not about that.

00:12:51.620 --> 00:12:55.620
If he was the thief, he would've 
already left after stealing the data.

00:12:55.620 --> 00:12:58.920
A criminal doesn't remain 
at the scene of the crime.

00:12:58.920 --> 00:13:01.210
That's true, but...

00:13:02.090 --> 00:13:04.650
Can't you build the program again?

00:13:04.650 --> 00:13:06.500
It's not that simple.

00:13:06.500 --> 00:13:10.270
Building a program is like 
holding a live concert.

00:13:10.270 --> 00:13:14.770
There's a lot of ad-libbing, so 
it's impossible to recreate it.

00:13:14.770 --> 00:13:18.430
So our only option is to find the thief?

00:13:18.780 --> 00:13:22.780
But the thief didn't leave 
any evidence behind.

00:13:22.780 --> 00:13:24.510
Even the fingerprints have been wiped clean.

00:13:24.720 --> 00:13:28.160
If there are no leads, how 
can we find the criminal?

00:13:29.030 --> 00:13:30.800
What is it, Bruno?

00:13:31.050 --> 00:13:33.860
One of the cup noodles is missing.

00:13:33.860 --> 00:13:36.590
What?  My cup noodles?

00:13:53.020 --> 00:13:54.850
I found the thief's fingerprint!

00:13:55.850 --> 00:14:00.320
While stealing the data, the thief 
was also eating the cup noodles.

00:14:00.320 --> 00:14:01.290
What?

00:14:01.290 --> 00:14:02.240
Are you serious?

00:14:02.240 --> 00:14:06.760
The criminal couldn't tear the 
cellophane, so he took off his gloves.

00:14:10.330 --> 00:14:12.570
Are you really going to do this, Yusei?

00:14:12.570 --> 00:14:13.570
Yeah.

00:14:13.570 --> 00:14:18.040
We can identify the thief by searching for 
this fingerprint in Security's database.

00:14:18.040 --> 00:14:22.610
But Security's database is 
protected by a powerful firewall.

00:14:22.610 --> 00:14:25.940
If they trace our hack, we'll be arrested.

00:14:26.440 --> 00:14:31.450
If we relay our hacking connection through 
servers around the world, we have five minutes.

00:14:34.150 --> 00:14:36.770
Bruno, can you break in within five minutes?

00:14:36.770 --> 00:14:38.440
Hopefully.

00:14:38.940 --> 00:14:41.180
Do you want us to stop, Jack?

00:14:42.400 --> 00:14:45.460
I leave Jack Atlas's fate to you!

00:14:45.460 --> 00:14:47.660
Don't hit me if I fail.

00:14:47.660 --> 00:14:49.430
Of course I'll hit you!

00:14:50.140 --> 00:14:53.100
Here we go!  Begin access!

00:14:57.040 --> 00:14:58.710
The trace has started.

00:14:58.710 --> 00:15:00.250
Can you do it?

00:15:00.250 --> 00:15:03.210
I think so.  It's a simple system.

00:15:03.930 --> 00:15:05.680
I don't fully understand, but...

00:15:05.680 --> 00:15:08.430
This guy is incredible.

00:15:09.650 --> 00:15:10.880
All right!

00:15:10.880 --> 00:15:13.120
If I pass the next one, 
we're in the database!

00:15:17.860 --> 00:15:19.380
What's this?

00:15:19.380 --> 00:15:21.330
It's suddenly a duel screen.

00:15:21.330 --> 00:15:23.100
This is the endgame of a duel!

00:15:23.570 --> 00:15:24.890
I see.

00:15:24.890 --> 00:15:28.290
The Public Maintenance Department uses 
the endgame of a duel as a password.

00:15:28.290 --> 00:15:31.410
If we don't solve this, 
we can't move forward?

00:15:31.410 --> 00:15:33.110
That's right.

00:15:33.110 --> 00:15:34.610
Four minutes left.

00:15:34.810 --> 00:15:37.580
We have to solve it within the time limit.

00:15:38.050 --> 00:15:39.920
The status is...

00:15:40.590 --> 00:15:44.690
The opponent has 2300 life points.  
We have 1000 life points.

00:15:44.690 --> 00:15:47.580
The opponent has five monsters on its field.

00:15:47.580 --> 00:15:50.570
In its Spell and Trap Card 
Zone, it has one set card

00:15:50.570 --> 00:15:53.530
and the activated Continuous 
Spell The Dark Door.

00:15:54.410 --> 00:15:56.710
Tragoedia is on our field.

00:15:56.710 --> 00:16:00.740
It gains 600 attack points 
for every card in our hand.

00:16:00.740 --> 00:16:02.720
We have six cards in our hand.

00:16:02.720 --> 00:16:05.080
Therefore, it has 3600 attack points.

00:16:05.960 --> 00:16:09.050
It says, "You must win during this turn."

00:16:09.050 --> 00:16:12.670
Our main worry is the set card on its field.

00:16:12.670 --> 00:16:16.700
We have to reduce the opponent's 
life points to zero this turn.

00:16:16.700 --> 00:16:18.870
All right, I got it!  Leave it to me!

00:16:21.350 --> 00:16:24.350
Since I have a monster 
with 3600 attack points

00:16:24.350 --> 00:16:27.390
and Shooting Star Bow - 
Ceal, the answer is simple!

00:16:27.390 --> 00:16:31.360
I equip the Equip Spell Shooting 
Star Bow - Ceal on Green Gadget!

00:16:31.360 --> 00:16:34.270
It loses 1000 attack points!

00:16:35.240 --> 00:16:38.640
Go, Tragoedia!  Attack Green Gadget!

00:16:40.940 --> 00:16:44.580
I activate the trap Mirror Force.

00:16:48.950 --> 00:16:50.650
What?

00:16:51.130 --> 00:16:56.660
Due to The Dark Door's effect, 
both players can only attack once.

00:16:56.660 --> 00:16:58.400
We can't win this turn.

00:16:58.400 --> 00:17:01.730
Crow, how dare you waste precious time!

00:17:01.730 --> 00:17:02.810
What?

00:17:02.810 --> 00:17:05.010
But we learned something.

00:17:05.010 --> 00:17:07.840
We know that the set card is Mirror Force.

00:17:07.840 --> 00:17:11.050
Mirror Force will completely 
destroy us if we attack.

00:17:11.050 --> 00:17:12.250
That's trouble!

00:17:12.750 --> 00:17:14.810
I can't watch your pathetic dueling!

00:17:17.130 --> 00:17:19.730
That's what you get for 
being sneaky and equipping

00:17:19.730 --> 00:17:22.470
an Equip Spell on the enemy 
to lower its attack points!

00:17:22.470 --> 00:17:26.060
A duel is about pushing 
through with your own power!

00:17:26.060 --> 00:17:28.890
I equip the Equip Spell Axe of Despair!

00:17:29.060 --> 00:17:31.480
Tragoedia has 4000 attack points!

00:17:31.480 --> 00:17:33.550
Go, Tragoedia!

00:17:33.550 --> 00:17:35.230
Attack Green Gadget!

00:17:36.800 --> 00:17:40.170
I activate the trap Mirror Force.

00:17:44.010 --> 00:17:47.150
Did you forget that the 
card was Mirror Force?

00:17:47.150 --> 00:17:49.980
I was testing to see if 
they changed the set card!

00:17:50.200 --> 00:17:52.980
We can't waste time!

00:17:52.980 --> 00:17:55.280
You can't talk to me like that!

00:17:55.280 --> 00:17:56.970
We have less than two minutes.

00:17:56.970 --> 00:17:58.560
Our next attempt will be our final chance.

00:17:59.050 --> 00:18:00.900
Will you let me try?

00:18:00.900 --> 00:18:01.760
What?

00:18:02.510 --> 00:18:03.490
Can you do it?

00:18:03.930 --> 00:18:05.060
Yeah.

00:18:05.060 --> 00:18:08.590
The only memories I have left 
are about D-Wheels and dueling.

00:18:08.590 --> 00:18:11.200
Besides, this might trigger my memories.

00:18:13.430 --> 00:18:15.920
Okay.  Do it, Bruno.

00:18:19.610 --> 00:18:21.610
Yusei, you can't count on him!

00:18:21.610 --> 00:18:23.810
Stop complaining!  There's no time!

00:18:29.260 --> 00:18:32.690
Can you solve this difficult 
problem in only two minutes?

00:18:33.920 --> 00:18:34.660
Here I go!

00:18:36.970 --> 00:18:40.600
The first problem is Mirror Force.

00:18:41.070 --> 00:18:43.300
I can't let that card activate.

00:18:44.470 --> 00:18:48.040
The only one that can stop Mirror Force is...

00:18:48.430 --> 00:18:53.190
Only Ancient Gear Soldier can stop 
traps from activating during battle.

00:18:53.780 --> 00:18:57.010
But Ancient Gear Soldier 
is on the opponent's field.

00:18:57.180 --> 00:18:59.830
I'll use its effect.

00:18:59.830 --> 00:19:05.520
Due to Tragoedia's effect, I send a card 
in my hand to the graveyard once a turn.

00:19:05.520 --> 00:19:09.990
I gain control of my opponent's monster 
whose Level is the same as the monster I discarded.

00:19:09.990 --> 00:19:13.390
But Ancient Gear Soldier's Level is 4.

00:19:14.680 --> 00:19:18.870
I only have Level 6 Alector, 
Sovereign of Birds in my hand.

00:19:18.870 --> 00:19:22.140
But I have a card named Cost Down.

00:19:22.990 --> 00:19:29.670
By discarding a card from my hand, Cost Down 
reduces the Level of all monsters in my hand by 2.

00:19:29.670 --> 00:19:33.130
That will make Alector's Level equal 4!

00:19:33.130 --> 00:19:34.290
Exactly!

00:19:34.290 --> 00:19:37.430
I activate Cost Down from my hand!

00:19:37.430 --> 00:19:42.920
I send Remove Trap to the graveyard to 
decrease Alcector's Level from 6 to 4.

00:19:42.920 --> 00:19:45.120
Next, due to Tragoedia's effect,

00:19:45.120 --> 00:19:49.490
I send Alector to the graveyard to 
gain control of Ancient Gear Soldier!

00:19:51.470 --> 00:19:52.730
I see.

00:19:52.730 --> 00:19:56.130
Now equip Axe of Despair 
and attack Green Gadget!

00:19:56.130 --> 00:19:57.290
No, not yet.

00:19:57.290 --> 00:19:58.120
What?

00:19:58.120 --> 00:19:59.680
Yusei's right.

00:19:59.680 --> 00:20:04.680
Even if we use Axe of Despair to increase 
Ancient Gear Soldier's attack points...

00:20:04.680 --> 00:20:10.920
...and then use Shooting Star Bow - Ceal to 
lower Green Gadget's attack points to 400...

00:20:10.920 --> 00:20:13.630
...we can only deal 1900 points of damage.

00:20:13.630 --> 00:20:14.920
That won't end the game.

00:20:14.920 --> 00:20:16.210
Then what should we do?

00:20:16.210 --> 00:20:18.140
Check the screen again.

00:20:18.140 --> 00:20:20.650
There's one thing we're forgetting.

00:20:20.650 --> 00:20:23.700
It's this effect!

00:20:23.700 --> 00:20:25.030
I see.

00:20:25.030 --> 00:20:28.300
But Stronghold has 3000 attack points.

00:20:28.490 --> 00:20:33.490
But Stronghold only has 3000 
attack points when Green Gadget,

00:20:33.490 --> 00:20:37.840
Yellow Gadget and Red 
Gadget are on the field.

00:20:37.840 --> 00:20:41.680
Without all three, it has 0 attack points.

00:20:41.680 --> 00:20:42.890
I see victory!

00:20:44.700 --> 00:20:47.760
I discard Shooting Star 
Bow - Ceal from my hand

00:20:47.760 --> 00:20:50.830
to activate the spell card 
Tribute to the Doomed!

00:20:52.430 --> 00:20:54.430
I destroy Green Gadget!

00:20:56.810 --> 00:20:59.780
Stronghold's attack points become 0!

00:21:01.720 --> 00:21:03.710
Then I equip Axe of Despair!

00:21:03.710 --> 00:21:07.380
Ancient Gear Soldier's 
attack points become 2300!

00:21:10.080 --> 00:21:12.580
Go, Ancient Gear Soldier!

00:21:12.580 --> 00:21:14.080
Attack Stronghold!

00:21:26.700 --> 00:21:28.040
We did it!

00:21:28.670 --> 00:21:30.630
Well done, Bruno!

00:21:30.960 --> 00:21:33.230
We have to check the fingerprint quickly!

00:21:38.200 --> 00:21:39.460
That's...

00:21:39.460 --> 00:21:40.410
Do you know him?

00:21:40.410 --> 00:21:43.180
He's the Vice Director of the 
Public Maintenance Department.

00:21:43.880 --> 00:21:45.440
It's Yeager.

00:22:09.590 --> 00:22:14.270
The small cliff floats on the Milky Way

00:22:14.270 --> 00:22:19.280
The sights I see are different 
than what I imagined

00:22:19.560 --> 00:22:24.180
Were you able to move on from the past?

00:22:24.180 --> 00:22:29.190
The answer isn't no, but 
there's something missing

00:22:29.390 --> 00:22:34.060
The cruel god tests us

00:22:34.360 --> 00:22:41.000
Let's fill the emptiness 
and head to the next stage

00:22:41.000 --> 00:22:44.870
If you ask me "What's our relationship?"

00:22:44.870 --> 00:22:50.740
We're more than friends... 
but that's not quite right

00:22:50.910 --> 00:22:54.660
Bond is the proper word

00:22:54.660 --> 00:23:00.640
As we fight, we understand each other

00:23:00.640 --> 00:23:03.610
"Where are you right now?"  "On Earth"

00:23:03.610 --> 00:23:05.840
Because I'm not an astronaut

00:23:05.840 --> 00:23:10.520
I have no problems when 
I'm below the ozone layer

00:23:10.810 --> 00:23:13.380
"I know, I'm coming right away."

00:23:13.380 --> 00:23:16.850
You want to party until the morning

00:23:16.850 --> 00:23:20.090
At our special place
